postman=[
('Requests and responses','Postman helps inspect HTTP messages. A request asks for work; a response gives a status, headers and sometimes a body.','Request: GET /books/17\nWorked response: 200 OK\nBody: {"id":17,"title":"Moon"}','The response describes book 17. This is a worked message, not a request sent by the lesson.','Identify the method, path and response body.','Reading a sample response does not prove a real service will return it.','Which part is the request method?','GET','Moon'),
('Read a URL','A URL identifies a destination. Its scheme, host, path and query parts have different roles.','https://practice.test/books?title=Moon\nScheme: https\nHost: practice.test\nPath: /books\nQuery: title=Moon','The query carries a search value. practice.test is a fictional host for reading the example.','Separate the parts of a second fictional URL.','Do not send requests to a system you are not authorised to use.','Which part contains the search value?','The query','The scheme'),
('GET reads a resource','GET asks for a representation of a resource. It should not be designed as a hidden command to delete or charge something.','GET /books/17 HTTP/1.1\nHost: practice.test\nAccept: application/json','The client asks for book 17 and says it can accept JSON. The Accept header describes a preferred response format.','Write a GET request for book 22.','Do not put private secrets in URLs; URLs can appear in logs.','What does Accept describe?','Preferred response content','The request password'),
('POST submits data','POST sends data to a resource for processing. Many APIs use it to create something, according to that API\'s contract.','POST /notes HTTP/1.1\nHost: practice.test\nContent-Type: application/json\n\n{"text":"Read chapter one"}','The body contains a fictional note. Content-Type says the sent body is JSON. No note is actually created here.','Change the fictional text and check the JSON quotes.','Never press Send against a live write endpoint merely to see what happens.','What does Content-Type describe here?','The sent body format','The response status only'),
('PUT PATCH and DELETE','Methods have different intended meanings. PUT commonly replaces a resource representation; PATCH changes part; DELETE requests removal.','PUT /notes/3 -> replace the note representation\nPATCH /notes/3 -> apply a partial change\nDELETE /notes/3 -> request removal','The API documentation must explain the exact body and behaviour. A delete example is a plan, not permission to delete real data.','Choose a method for changing only a note\'s color under a documented partial-update API.','A method name alone does not tell you all the service\'s business rules.','Which method usually applies a partial change?','PATCH','GET'),
('Understand status families','The first status-code digit groups the result. 2xx means success; 4xx indicates a client-side request issue; 5xx indicates a server-side failure.','200 OK: successful read\n404 Not Found: requested item missing\n500 Internal Server Error: server failed','The code gives a broad result. Read the documented error body for more detail.','Classify 201 and 403 by their first digit.','Do not assume every non-200 response is a server crash.','Which code indicates a missing resource?','404','500'),
('Read JSON safely','JSON is a text format for structured data. Object keys and string values use double quotes.','{"title":"Moon","pages":24,"available":true}','The object has text, a number and a boolean. pages is a number because it is not quoted.','Add an author string with valid commas and quotes.','JSON does not allow comments or trailing commas in its standard form.','Which field contains a number?','pages','title'),
('Use variables for repeatable requests','A Postman variable can hold a reusable value such as a base URL. The selected scope controls which value is used.','Request URL: {{baseUrl}}/books/17\nPractice baseUrl: https://practice.test','Changing the variable lets a collection target a different approved environment without editing every request.','Explain why you must inspect the active environment before sending.','Do not accidentally switch a harmless practice request to a live write environment.','What does {{baseUrl}} represent?','A variable value','A literal required hostname'),
('Keep credentials private','Some real APIs need credentials. Use the tool\'s appropriate local or secret storage and authorised access; do not copy real tokens into examples or public collections.','Public collection: request shape and non-secret examples\nPrivate authorised setup: credentials supplied separately','The request documentation can be shared without publishing the secret. Postman cloud sync and collaboration have their own privacy settings.','Identify which parts of an example are safe to share.','Removing a token from a new export does not revoke a token that was already leaked.','What should be excluded from a public collection?','Real tokens','A documented method name'),
('Write a response check','A Postman response script can assert facts about the last response. pm is provided by Postman\'s script environment.','pm.test("status is OK", function () {\n  pm.response.to.have.status(200);\n});','This check passes only if the actual response status is 200. It belongs in Postman, not this site\'s JavaScript runner.','Write a separate check for the expected Content-Type header.','A status check alone does not verify every field in a response body.','What does this script check?','Response status','Every book title'),
('Check a response field','A body check should use the contract for that request. Read JSON and assert the field you need.','pm.test("book has a title", function () {\n  const book = pm.response.json();\n  pm.expect(book.title).to.be.a("string");\n});','For a documented JSON book response, the test checks that title is a string. A non-JSON body makes parsing fail.','Add a check that pages is a number.','Do not parse every response as JSON without checking the endpoint\'s contract.','What type is required for title?','String','Array'),
('Organise and review a collection','A collection groups related requests and examples. Review its target URLs, scripts and exported data before sharing or running it.','Collection: Library reads\nRequests: find a book, list books\nExamples: success and missing-book response\nReview: no real credentials or private data','The collection documents both a normal result and an error case. Examples remain illustrative until checked against a real authorised service.','Write a short collection description that states its purpose.','A downloaded collection can contain scripts; inspect it before running.','What should you review before running a collection?','URLs, scripts and data','Only its cover image'),
]
C('postman','Postman helps people inspect and test HTTP requests. Learn methods, URLs, status codes, JSON and response checks through worked messages that do not need a live API.','No account or API service is needed to read these examples. practice.test is fictional. Postman scripts require Postman\'s own environment and do not run in the website playground.','https://learning.postman.com/docs/getting-started/overview/',[L(*r) for r in postman])

vscode=[
('An editor helps you write files','Visual Studio Code is a code editor. It helps you read and change files, but it is not the same thing as a browser or every language\'s runtime.','Editor: write index.html\nBrowser: display index.html\nSeparate runtime: needed for languages such as Python','Each tool has a different job. This course focuses on the editor and safe local practice files.','Explain which tool displays the HTML page.','Installing the editor does not install every programming language.','What is VS Code primarily?','A code editor','Every language runtime'),
('Open a practice folder','Opening a folder gives the editor a workspace for related files. Use a new folder made only for learning.','club-site/\n  index.html\n  style.css','The Explorer can show the page and stylesheet together. A folder name helps you recognise the project.','Create a notes.txt file inside the practice folder.','Do not open a sensitive or unfamiliar project and immediately trust or run all its tasks.','Why open a folder?','To work with related project files','To publish the site automatically'),
('Use the Command Palette','The Command Palette searches editor actions by name. It is useful when you do not remember a menu location.','Open the Command Palette\nSearch: Format Document\nRead the command name before choosing it','The palette helps find actions. A command\'s availability can depend on the current file and installed extensions.','Find the command for changing the color theme.','Read a command before running it; similar names can do different things.','What does the Command Palette search?','Editor actions','Only file contents'),
('Save and recognise file types','A file extension helps the editor choose language support. Saving changes writes them to disk; an unsaved tab can differ from the saved file.','index.html -> HTML\nstyle.css -> CSS\nnotes.txt -> plain text','The extension communicates the file type. The editor\'s language mode can also be selected manually.','Save a small HTML page and open it in a browser.','A file named page.html.txt is still a text file by its final extension.','Which name is an HTML file?','page.html','page.html.txt'),
('Search within a file','Find locates matching text in the current file. Check match-case and whole-word settings when results seem surprising.','Text: Moon moon moonlight\nSearch: moon\nMatch case on: lowercase matches only\nWhole word on: excludes moonlight','Search settings change what counts as a match.','Predict the matches with both options on.','An empty result can come from a filter, not from missing text.','What does whole-word search avoid here?','Matching moon inside moonlight','Finding the word moon'),
('Search across the project','Workspace search finds text in several files. Review the included and excluded paths before trusting the result.','Search target: club-site files\nQuery: Reading club\nPossible matches: index.html and notes.txt','The results show file names and matching lines. They help you find all visible uses of a phrase.','Limit a search to HTML files.','Excluded or ignored files may not appear in search results.','Does a workspace search always include every file on disk?','No','Yes'),
('Replace with a preview','Replace changes text. Review each match or the preview before applying many changes at once.','Old label: Save book\nNew label: Bookmark book\nReview: check every matched file before replacing','A small preview helps avoid changing unrelated sentences or variable names.','Find one case that should not be changed with the others.','Do not run a broad replacement without reviewing its scope.','What should happen before Replace All?','Review the matches','Publish immediately'),
('Formatting keeps layout consistent','A formatter adjusts layout such as indentation. It should preserve the intended program behaviour. The formatter used depends on the language and setup.','Before: const score={value:8};\nAfter:  const score = { value: 8 };','The spaces improve readability; the object still stores the same value.','Format a small practice file and review the diff.','Formatting is not the same as fixing every program bug.','What does formatting mainly change?','Code layout','The intended business rules'),
('Workspace settings','Workspace settings apply to the project. A .vscode/settings.json file can record a few agreed editor choices.','{\n  "editor.wordWrap": "on",\n  "editor.formatOnSave": true\n}','Word wrapping makes long lines easier to see. Format on save uses an available configured formatter.','Try wordWrap off and compare the view.','Do not commit private paths or secrets into shared workspace settings.','Where do these project settings commonly live?','.vscode/settings.json','A public password file'),
('The integrated terminal','The integrated terminal is a real shell inside the editor window. Its commands can change files just like any other terminal.','Read the current directory\nRun a harmless version command if the tool is installed\nExample: git --version','The terminal is convenient but still powerful. Know which project folder it is using.','Compare the terminal path with the folder open in Explorer.','Do not paste an unfamiliar command just because it is shown near editor instructions.','Is the integrated terminal only a pretend shell?','No, it runs real commands','Yes'),
('Extensions and workspace trust','Extensions add editor features. Workspace Trust helps decide whether code in a folder may activate potentially risky features.','New downloaded project\nFirst: read its files in a restricted state\nThen: trust only when you understand the source and needed actions','The decision is about the project source, not whether its icon looks familiar. Install only extensions you need from a trusted publisher.','Explain why an unknown folder should not automatically run tasks.','An extension can have significant access; avoid installing random ones for every tutorial.','What should guide workspace trust?','Whether you understand and trust the project','Its folder color'),
('Debug one step at a time','A debugger can pause a supported program and let you inspect values. A breakpoint marks a place to pause. Setup depends on the language runtime.','Breakpoint before: total = price * count\nInspect: price is 3, count is 2\nStep over: total becomes 6','The debugger makes the program\'s state visible one step at a time. It does not decide what the correct result should be.','Predict total before stepping over the calculation.','Do not confuse stepping through code with proving every input is correct.','What does a breakpoint do?','Pauses at a chosen place','Deletes that line'),
]
C('vscode','Visual Studio Code helps you edit project files. Learn folders, search, formatting, settings and safe terminal use through a small static-page workspace.','Use a new local practice folder. Menu names may vary slightly by platform. No account, extensions or paid service are needed just to read these lessons.','https://code.visualstudio.com/docs/getstarted/getting-started',[L(*r) for r in vscode])
